# Hemp Wool — vanilla white_wool's own weave, retoned to hemp fibre.
#
# The MATRIX below is vanilla `block/white_wool.png` extracted verbatim: 40 tones of
# dithered noise that would be pointless to redraw and impossible to improve by hand.
# Only the PALETTE is ours. Each vanilla tone was mapped by luminance onto the ramp
# between hemp_fiber.png's two body colours — C4A985 (mid) and E0CBB3 (highlight) — so
# the block's every pixel is a colour the fibre item already uses, and the relative
# spacing of vanilla's shading is preserved exactly.
#
# To retone: change the two endpoint colours and re-derive the ramp linearly by
# luminance. Do NOT hand-edit individual entries — they are a monotone ramp and will
# band if they stop being one.

@palette hemp_fibre
. = none
1 = C4A985
2 = C5AA86
3 = C5AB87
4 = C6AB88
5 = C7AC89
6 = C7AD8A
7 = C8AD8B
8 = C8AE8C
9 = C9AF8D
a = CAB08E
b = CAB18F
c = CBB190
d = CCB291
e = CCB393
f = CEB595
g = CEB595
h = CEB696
j = CFB798
k = D0B899
m = D1B99B
n = D1B99B
p = D3BB9D
q = D3BC9E
r = D5BDA0
s = D5BEA1
t = D6BFA3
u = D7C0A4
v = D8C1A5
w = D9C2A7
x = D9C3A8
y = DAC4AA
z = DBC5AB
A = DCC6AC
B = DCC7AD
C = DDC7AE
D = DDC8AF
E = DEC8AF
F = DFC9B1
G = DFCAB2
H = E0CBB3

